================================================================================

The Mechanism
> (Truncate & Overwrite):

Opens the target file with the O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC flags.

If the file exists, the filesystem immediately sets its file length to 0 (truncation), dropping prior content before writing the new stream.

If the file does not exist, it creates a new regular file.

>> (Append):

Opens the target file with the O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_APPEND flags.

Does not modify existing contents. The file offset is automatically moved to the end of the file before every write operation.

